---
---`GET /api/billing/subscription`
---@param input? archil.GetBillingSubscriptionRequest
---@return archil.ApiResponseBillingSubscription? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:get_billing_subscription(input) end

---Get a billing period's statement
---
---Returns a billing period's statement as billing itself states it: `lines`, each line invoiced for the period or previewed for its end (a fixed fee, a meter's usage billed past its grants, a credit taken off, anything else under its own name), and `billedCost`, their sum, which is what the period invoices or would if it ended now. On the current period also `credits`, the grants the account still draws on, and a projection to the period end at the recent daily pace. Nothing here is derived from the plan's terms: a plan billing can express, this route reports. Money is in dollars to the cent, before tax. A line is before discounts, as billing reports it, and what a reward takes off follows as an `other` line named `Discount`: off each line previewed for the period end, and off each invoice as a whole (its total under its lines' sum), on the span of the invoice's fixed fee when it has one, else of its first line on the period. So the sum is what the period invoiced, or will.
---
---`GET /api/billing/summary`
---Errors: BadRequest.
---@param input? archil.GetBillingSummaryRequest
---@return archil.ApiResponseBillingSummary? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:get_billing_summary(input) end

---Get metered usage and its cost over a window
---
---Returns what the account's meters recorded over a window, for the window as a whole and per interval, in each meter's own unit (such as vCPU-hours, GiB-hours, GiB-months or calls), and what that usage comes to at the account's rates, per meter and in total, before any grant and fixed fee: the cost of what was used, not what will be invoiced, which `/api/billing/summary` reports. The meters are the catalog's metered features, so a meter added there is reported from then on. A meter's rate is the price of the plan item its usage is billed from: the meter's own item, or the credit system whose rate card names it, at the plan's own prices and overrides; a meter the plan does not price has a zero rate, and a tiered item is priced at its first tier. Usage reaches billing once per reporter interval from every region, so an interval's figures can still grow for a few minutes after it ends, longer if a region's reporter is behind. The default window is the seven days (hourly: 24 hours) up to now; a window may be at most 31 days, and is widened to whole intervals. Money is in dollars, to the cent.
---
---`GET /api/billing/usage`
